-- title:
--   Level Mpᵃ⁺¹ divisor-expansion field is generated by j(q^pᵃ⁺¹)
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, $p$ a prime, $a$ a natural number, and suppose $p \nmid M$. Work inside the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$, and for a nonzero natural number $N$ write $\mathrm{jqN}(N) = \mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,N\,\mathrm{jq}$, the image of the $j$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ under the ring homomorphism that multiplies all Hahn-series exponents by $N$ (substitution $q \mapsto q^{N}$). For such $N$, `modularFunctionFieldFull N` is the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of all $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,\mathrm{jq}$ with $d$ a nonzero divisor of $N$. The assertion is the equality of intermediate fields $$\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}(M p^{a+1}) = \mathbb{Q}\bigl(\{\mathrm{jqN}(p^{a+1})\} \cup \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}(M p^{a})\bigr),$$ where on the right the element $\mathrm{jqN}(p^{a+1})$ is inserted into the carrier set of the level-$Mp^{a}$ field and the ℚ-adjoin of the resulting set is taken; that is, adjoining the single new expansion $j(q^{p^{a+1}})$ to the level-$Mp^{a}$ field already produces every $j(q^{d})$ with $d \mid M p^{a+1}$.
--
--   This is an induction step in the generation theory for the $q$-expansion model of the function field of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$: it reduces the divisor-expansion field at level $Mp^{a+1}$ to the level $Mp^{a}$ field together with the top $p$-power expansion. It is used in the construction of irreducible modular-polynomial data, in the production of Atkin–Lehner type automorphisms at primes not dividing the level, and in the computation of degeneracy and Hecke operators.
-- source:
